    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All 58 tests pass, build succeeds. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI converted owner deletion to a soft-delete. `DELETE /api/owners/{id}` now flags the record and retains it, `GET` still returns it with `deleted: true`, and the create endpoint's duplicate/identity checks ignore deleted owners.\n\n**Changes made:**\n\n1. **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added a `deleted` boolean field (`@Column(name = \"deleted\")`), initialized to `false` so a newly built owner is not deleted, plus getter/setter.\n\n2. **`function/owner/DeleteOwner.java`** \u2014 instead of `ownerRepository.delete(owner)`, it now sets `owner.setDeleted(true)` and saves, retaining the row.\n\n3. **Duplicate/identity checks** \u2014 `CheckOwnerIdentityUnique`, `CheckOwnerHouseholdUnique`, and `AssignPossibleDuplicate` now skip any existing owner where `deleted` is true, so a normally-blocking duplicate is allowed when the only match was soft-deleted.\n\n4. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `deleted` boolean to the `Owner` response schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` carries it and MapStruct maps `Owner.deleted \u2192 OwnerDto.deleted` by name (surfacing `$.deleted` in the GET response).\n\n5. **Schema/seed SQL** \u2014 added a `deleted BOOLEAN` column to the `owners` table in all four dialect schemas (hsqldb, h2, postgres, mysql; `ddl-auto=none` so the column must exist in `schema.sql`), and appended `FALSE` to the positional hsqldb seed inserts to keep the value/column counts aligned.\n\nCp46's two new tests pass, and the full suite (58 tests) is green.\n\nNote: mysql's `data.sql` seed inserts were already inconsistent with the mysql schema's column count before this change and aren't exercised by the test suite (which uses the hsqldb profile), so I left them untouched rather than widen the scope.",
